    fix(tests): stub path-memory recall in topology-escalation test (env-dependent failure)
    
    test_complete_map_fact_stops_repeat_topology_escalation never stubbed
    duckbrain_client.recall, so a live local DuckBrain holding real
    /world/path/* records from actual runs let NAV-MEM legally replay a
    proven route (['LEFT']) instead of the ROM-derived plan (['DOWN']).
    CI passed only because its store read misses. Stub recall to an empty
    list — the test targets ROM topology resolution, not path memory.
    
    Same class fixed in test_world_topology_refresh.py:
    test_teacher_missing_facts_become_next_cycle_world_targets failed on a
    clean tree at this host because a live local DuckBrain answered the
    pre-teacher NAV-MEM consult; stubbed recall to [] for the same reason.
    
